{"key":"FeaturesWindow","text":"## FeaturesWindow\n\nThe **Features Window** is the product map: everything the OS can do, grouped\nby purpose, with a status dot on each line and a chip that opens that\nfeature's Help. Right-click any line to request a change or report a bug\nagainst it.\n\n---\n\n@layout\nTitle Bar | 0.50, 0.04 | The left buttons toggle wrapped text, the status pane, and the bug and request pills.\nTabs | 0.50, 0.12 | AI Design, Game Design, OS and Wishlist, each with a live entry count.\nStatus Pane | 0.10, 0.55 | Stable, Beta, Planned and Wishlist with counts. Click one to filter; click the empty space to clear. Drag the divider to resize.\nFeature List | 0.60, 0.55 | One row per feature: status dot, a blue window chip, the descriptor, and any linked bug or request pills.\n\n---\n\n### Reading the list\n\n- **Status dot** — hover for the word: Stable, Beta, Planned or Wishlist\n- **Window chip** — click to open that window's Help; hover for a moment to preview its screenshot, click the preview to zoom\n- **Bug and request pills** — click to open the linked report\n\n### Filing against a feature\n\n- **Right-click a row** — *Request a change…* or *Report a bug…*, pre-filled and permanently linked to that feature\n\n### Where it comes from\n\n- The list is Features.md. In the browser it loads from GitHub; if it has not been published yet an amber banner offers **Publish to GitHub**\n- **Right-click the title bar** — Save to GitHub or Export\n\n### Shortcuts\n\n- None; the tabs and pane are click-driven.\n\n### Status: Stable\n### Purpose: OS\n\n---","screenshot":""}